  writeup: "At 14:05, DLP flagged derek@nexxuss.example uploading 3.8 GB — source code and a customer list — to personal cloud storage (T1567.002), after a 13:55 on-site interactive sign-in on his managed laptop and a 14:02 bulk clone of three private repositories. HR shows Derek resigned and is joining a competitor, Palanthas Labs, with access still active during notice. Consistent with intentional exfiltration by an insider. Handled quietly: escalated to HR, legal and Sturm through a restricted channel; DLP, identity, repo and upload logs preserved under chain of custody. Kept separate from the same-day mailbox takeover (VOO-4035). Could not be confirmed: what Derek did with the files inside his personal account, which the SOC can't see.",
